# Security headers (#105). Cloudflare Workers serves this file natively — one
# of the reasons Workers was picked over Pages (docs/CLOUDFLARE.md).
#
# The stakes here are genuinely low and that is why this is a short file rather
# than a thorough one: static site, no auth, no forms, no cookies, no user
# input, no secrets in the client. The old site's one real attack surface, the
# PHP contact form, is gone by decision. This is hygiene and defense in depth,
# not a hole being closed.
#
# ## Two things are deliberately absent
#
# **Content-Security-Policy.** The site loads a YouTube iframe on project pages
# and the Cloudflare Insights beacon sitewide, so a CSP written by guesswork
# silently breaks embeds or analytics rather than failing loudly. Getting it
# right means shipping Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first and reading
# real reports, which needs real traffic — the site has only just started
# receiving any. Not guessed at here.
#
# **Strict-Transport-Security.** Additive and safe, but it is also a
# zone-level Cloudflare setting, and picking ONE of the two places is the whole
# point. Setting it here and at the edge is the drift this repo avoids
# everywhere else. Ali's call which. Whichever wins, don't reach for a long
# max-age with `preload` until the domain has been serving HTTPS happily for a
# while — `preload` is the one line here that is hard to walk back.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Branch previews must never be indexable, independent of whether `main` is
# public (#212). `live` (src/config/site.ts) governs robots.txt and the
# per-page <meta name="robots"> for the one build this site produces — it
# can't also answer "which hostname is this," because the build is static and
# the same output serves both aliwallick.com and every *.workers.dev preview.
# Only a per-host rule can draw that line, which is what this is.
#
# `:branch` matches any single label ahead of the account subdomain, so this
# covers every `<branch>-portfolio.ali-wallick.workers.dev` preview — not just
# main-portfolio, the one that's deliberately public for sharing — as
# defense-in-depth if a preview's Cloudflare Access gate is ever off. robots.txt
# still says `Allow` on these hosts; that's deliberate; a page has to be
# crawlable for a crawler to see this header and drop it from the index.
https://:branch.ali-wallick.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
